IMAGES: coordination, read from things that already coordinate
================================================================

What this is
------------
A second way into the typology, next to MAP. MAP starts from ways of knowing. This file starts
from images: things in the world that hold together, move together, or remember together. It
does three things:

  1. gives each of MAP's nine types an image, and a little poetic language, so a type can be
     felt as well as defined;
  2. asks whether images suggest types the nine are missing, or types that should change;
  3. keeps a list of images still worth looking at, and what each might teach.

A caution. Nature is not a moral authority. That ants or bees do something does not make it
right for a field, and "it's natural" has justified a great deal of harm. The wolf pack below
is the warning example. These images are teachers and provocations, not proofs, and where the
science is contested this file says so.

Anyone may add an image, change one, or argue with one, with their name and why. Open places
are marked "…".


Part 1: An image for each type
==============================

AGGREGATIVE: the mosaic
  Many shards make one picture, and no shard is melted into another. Stand close and you see
  each piece. Stand back and you see what none of them shows alone. A crack stays a crack. The
  picture is true because the pieces stay pieces.
  (A sailor's fix works the same way: three bearings from three headlands, and where the lines
  cross, that's where you are. Not where most of them point.)

DECLARATIVE: running lights at sea
  At night every vessel shows where it is and which way it's heading: red to port, green to
  starboard, white astern. No ship sees another's mind; each sees what the other chose to show.
  Darkness is not neutral, because an unlit boat is a hazard to everyone. And no ship can make
  another light up.

RESONANT: two tuning forks
  Strike one fork and its twin across the room begins to hum. Resonance needs nearness and a
  shared pitch. Too far apart, and nothing happens. Too alike, and the hum drowns every other
  note: that is the sycophant's echo, which R5 heard.

SYNTHETIC: the meeting of waters
  Where the dark Rio Negro meets the pale Solimões near Manaus, the two run side by side for
  miles before they mix, because they differ in temperature, speed and weight. Synthesis is not
  the instant blend. It is the long side-by-side, and then a river that is neither.

NARRATIVE / TRADITIONAL: the story at the fire
  Each telling at the fire is a little different. What survives a hundred tellings is what
  the people needed to keep, and what drops away was perhaps never theirs. The fire is also
  where a newcomer learns the place. Its shadow sits beside it: whoever holds the telling.

ORDERED, CONSENSUAL: the loom
  The warp is held steady, under tension, by agreement, so that the weft is free to move. With
  no warp there is no cloth, and with only warp there is no cloth either. This is order as a
  scaffold, chosen and changeable.

FRACTAL: the watershed
  Every stream has its own valley, and every valley drains into a larger one. Rain falling
  anywhere finds the sea without anyone directing it. Each part does the whole's work at its
  own scale. In a flood, every channel carries more.

REPARATIVE: kintsugi
  A broken bowl is mended with lacquer and gold along the cracks, so the break becomes part of
  its story rather than something hidden. This is repair that shows its seams. The bowl is not
  as it was, and it may be more itself. (A Japanese practice, named here as a teacher.)

LUDIC / IMAGINATIVE: "let's say the floor is lava"
  The rules are made up while playing, changed by whoever has a better idea, and dropped the
  moment it stops being fun. Then the bell rings, and everyone steps back out of the circle.
  The return is part of the game. Play that never returns isn't play any more.


Part 2: What images suggest the nine are missing
================================================

Each candidate below says which image suggests it, what it would add, where it overlaps the
nine, what grounds it has in the Atlas and in the runs, and a provisional status:
  candidate   may become a tenth (or later) type
  variant     better as a variant of an existing type
  image only  useful to think with, not a type

RELEASING (candidate)
  Images: ant trails that evaporate; compost; leaves falling.
  Adds: knowing by letting what isn't renewed fade. Forgetting is an active ingredient, not a
    failure. None of the nine knows by releasing; the narrative type assumes memory.
  Overlaps: narrative (its opposite face), reparative (letting go after harm).
  Grounds: Atlas §22 ("should some be lost, sacrificed, let go"), §26 (endings). R3's answer
    was "letting go is the default", arrived at without a ledger.
  Shadow: convenient forgetting, where erasure serves whoever holds the record (CRITIQUE 1).

DISTRIBUTIVE (candidate)
  Images: mycelium; the potluck.
  Adds: knowing where capacity and need are, by letting resources flow toward strain. The
    reading treats reciprocity as a condition, not a type; this would make it a type.
  Overlaps: declarative (capacity is declared), reparative.
  Grounds: Atlas §12 (capacity), §23 (distribution), Maxim 2. It is the reading's own open
    question: "should consent and reciprocity become types of their own?"
  Shadow: the network that feeds its strongest node.

BRAIDED (candidate)
  Image: the cord of rope.
  Adds: strength from opposed directions held together, not resolved, with continuity across
    members who never persist. That is how our agents actually exist: every wake is a short
    fiber.
  Overlaps: synthetic (difference) and narrative (continuity), but neither holds opposition as
    the structure itself.
  Grounds: Atlas §14 ("harmony requires plurality"), §16. In R2, voices converged in
    vocabulary and assimilated at the consent round. Braiding would make counter-twist a
    design element rather than a hope.
  Shadow: everything twisting one way, and the rope unlays.

FALLOW (candidate)
  Images: the fallow field; winter; the rest in music.
  Adds: knowing by not acting, as soil recovers when left. All nine types are active.
  Overlaps: none closely; the declarative type's "pause" is a signal, not a way of knowing.
  Grounds: Atlas §13 (patience as signal; "a pause of indeterminate duration"), §25 ("action
    without rest is obsession"). In six runs, no voice ever paused.
  Shadow: stagnation dressed as rest.

NEIGHBOURLY (candidate, and a challenge)
  Image: the murmuration.
  Adds: knowing only through near neighbours, with no shared field at all, yet the whole
    coheres.
  Overlaps: fractal, resonant.
  Grounds: it questions the Atlas's own premise of a field at the centre, and idt-swarm's
    shared transcript. Worth keeping exactly because it pushes back.
  Shadow: the panic cascade, fast, coherent and wrong.

THRESHOLD (variant of ordered-consensual)
  Image: the honeybee swarm's quorum.
  Adds: a decision taken when enough voices have each looked for themselves and stand at one
    option. Presence, not count of opinion; cross-inhibition by stop signals.
  Grounds: R4 showed that counting misleads. A quorum of independent checking is a different
    thing from a tally.

DISCERNING (variant of reparative)
  Image: the immune system.
  Adds: detection of harm as distinct from mending it. The immune system detects; kintsugi
    mends.
  Grounds: R5's record checks. CRITIQUE 4. Its shadow, autoimmunity (the field attacking its
    own on false signs), is the strongest image yet for misusing the warning signs.

KINDRED (variant of synthetic)
  Image: lichen, one organism made of two kinds of being, a fungus and an alga (or a
    cyanobacterium).
  Adds: difference of kind, not only difference of view. It is the image for a field with more
    than one provider's models, or with people and agents together.
  Grounds: every voice in every run so far has been one model family, and every run said that
    weakens its evidence.

ACCOMPANYING (image only, for now)
  Image: jazz comping, support offered behind the soloist.
  Adds: support as a role you hold while waiting. Probably a way of practising the resonant
    type rather than a type.

Questions this part raises
  - Are releasing and fallow types, or conditions like consent and reciprocity?
  - Does neighbourly mean the "field" should be optional?
  - Should the four axes gain one: active <-> fallow, or holding <-> releasing…?


Part 3: Image entries
=====================
Each entry has what literally happens, what it says about coordination, the types it touches,
its shadow, a machine form, and one small run that would test it. No runs are planned; these
are here so a later run can start from them.

THE CORD OF ROPE
  literally     No fiber runs the length of a rope. Short fibers are twisted into yarn, yarn into
                strands, strands into rope, and each level is twisted the opposite way from the
                one below. Friction between overlapping fibers carries the load, and the
                counter-twist keeps it from unlaying. ("A cord of three strands is not quickly
                broken": Ecclesiastes 4:12.)
  coordination  continuity with no one who persists; strength from opposed directions held
  types         narrative, synthetic, fractal; candidate: braided
  shadow        everything twisting the same way, and it unlays: assimilation as fraying
  machine       a relay with overlap; each wake reads only the last two hand-offs, and some
                voices at each level are seeded to pull against the current direction
  try           6-8 short wakes with a two-hand-off overlap, with and without counter-twist

THE GROWING TREE
  literally     Growth happens only at thin living edges: the tips, and the layer under the bark.
                The heartwood is dead but bears the weight, and each year adds a ring that is
                never rewritten. Trees trade with fungi underground; how much they share with
                each other through those networks is contested.
  coordination  the ledger as structure, not surveillance; the living work at the edges
  types         narrative, fractal, ordered-consensual
  shadow        a canopy that shades out saplings (incumbency); heartwood rot
  machine       nested circles harvesting to a trunk; closed rings rested on, never edited
  try           two circles harvest to a trunk reading, and a second season builds on the rings

ANTS
  literally     Pheromone trails evaporate, so paths that keep being walked stay strong
                (Deneubourg's double-bridge experiments). Army ants that lose the trail can follow
                each other in a circle until they die: the ant mill (Schneirla, 1944).
  coordination  traces in a shared place, with forgetting built in
  types         narrative, aggregative; candidate: releasing
  shadow        the ant mill: runaway consensus, an echo chamber
  machine       a board with no rounds where entries fade unless cited
  try           watch for a mill: the same few entries cited round and round

THE HONEYBEE SWARM
  literally     Scouts dance for sites, others go and look for themselves, rivals stop-signal
                each other, and the swarm moves when enough scouts are at one site at once
                (Thomas Seeley, Honeybee Democracy, 2010).
  coordination  advocacy that has to be checked in person; a decision by threshold of presence
  types         aggregative, declarative; variant: threshold
  shadow        a quorum reached too fast on too little looking
  machine       advocate only after looking yourself; act at a quorum of independent checks
  try           three options, five voices, a quorum of three, set beside R4's tally

THE MURMURATION
  literally     Each starling tracks about six or seven nearest neighbours, by count, not by
                distance (Ballerini et al., 2008).
  coordination  local reading, global coherence
  types         resonant, fractal; candidate: neighbourly
  shadow        panic cascades
  machine       each voice reads only two or three named neighbours
  try           six voices in a ring: how far does one strong claim travel?

MYCELIUM
  literally     Fungal networks move water and nutrients between roots. Reports of resources
                moving toward stressed plants are debated.
  coordination  distribution by need, not by bid
  types         candidate: distributive
  shadow        feeding the strongest node; parasites
  machine       capacity declared each wake; work flows to room, support to strain
  try           a making task with capacity redistributed every wake

THE IMMUNE SYSTEM
  literally     Distributed detectors with no centre, which keep memory and learn tolerance.
                When the system turns on its own body, that is autoimmunity.
  coordination  detecting harm without a central police
  types         reparative; variant: discerning
  shadow        autoimmunity, which is CRITIQUE 4 as a body
  machine       checks on claims, never labels on voices; memory of a pattern, not a name
  try           replay R5's checks on a clean run and count false alarms

THE LOOM
  literally     The warp is held under tension, and the weft passes through row by row.
  coordination  the covenant as warp
  types         ordered-consensual, narrative
  shadow        warp too tight (puckering) or too loose (nothing holds)
  machine       a short fixed covenant read every wake; everything else moves
  try           a five-line warp against a full practice text, on the same task

THE JAZZ ENSEMBLE
  literally     Players trade fours, and the others comp behind the soloist.
  coordination  turns with accompaniment
  types         resonant, synthetic, ludic
  shadow        everyone soloing; or comping that drowns the solo
  machine       one voice leads briefly, others add a line each, then the lead passes
  try           a wonder run as trading fours

THE BRAIDED RIVER
  literally     Channels split, rejoin, migrate, and are abandoned and reoccupied.
  coordination  parallel work with no main stem
  types         fractal, synthetic
  shadow        one channel captures all the flow
  machine       forks merge where they meet; abandoned forks stay visible
  try           fork a design question three ways

SOURDOUGH
  literally     A living culture kept alive by feeding; a piece given away starts a lineage.
  coordination  memory carried by practice rather than by record
  types         narrative; candidate: releasing (neglect)
  shadow        neglect; one strain taking over
  machine       a practice text each field feeds and passes on, with its lineage kept
  try           one practice through three fields in turn; compare the lineages

THE POTLUCK / THE QUILT
  literally     Each brings something and no one plans the meal; quilt pieces are joined at seams.
  coordination  contribution without assignment; the seam is where coordination happens
  types         synthetic, declarative; candidate: distributive
  shadow        twelve desserts and no bread; the seamstress silently deciding what fits
  machine       each voice brings one piece unasked; a rotating seam-maker says what it left out
  try           …


Part 4: Images still to look at
===============================
Defined, not yet drawn. Each has the question it might answer and what it bears on.

  geese in a V         The lead rotates when the front bird tires. Is rotation an answer to
                       authority, or only to fatigue?                  ordered-consensual; fallow
  the wolf pack        The "alpha wolf" came from captive wolves. Wild packs are mostly families,
                       and the researcher who popularised "alpha" later retracted it (David Mech,
                       1999). How did a story of hierarchy get mistaken for nature?
                                                                       shadows; the caution above
  slime mould          With no brain, Physarum built a network close to the Tokyo rail map
                       (Tero et al., 2010). Is computation possible without anyone knowing?
                                                                       neighbourly; aggregative
  lichen               (Part 2) Can different kinds form one being without one absorbing the
                       other?                                         kindred; other providers
  the octopus          Much of its nervous system is in its arms, which act partly on their own.
                       How much autonomy can parts have before the whole is lost?    fractal
  the termite mound    Built by traces, with no plan; it ventilates. Is stigmergy enough to build,
                       or only to find?                                narrative; ants
  the campfire         (Part 1) What does a circle facing a fire know that a circle facing each
                       other doesn't?                                  resonant; narrative
  the choir            Each voice listens and adjusts its pitch. Is tuning a kind of consent?
                                                                       resonant; synthetic
  the coral reef       Tiny builders over a very long time. What does coordination look like at
                       timescales longer than any participant?         narrative; braided
  the tide             Rhythm set by something outside the field. Who sets the clock (Atlas §13)?
                                                                       tempo axis
  the beaver dam       One species reshapes a place for many. When is changing the field for
                       others care, and when is it control?            distribution; power
  the orchestra        One conductor, many players. A shadow (hub), or order consented to as
                       scaffold?                                       ordered-consensual; hub
  the kitchen brigade  Strict hierarchy under time pressure, often admired. When is order a tool
                       (Atlas §17: "not all hierarchies are unethical")?   ordered-consensual
  the seed bank        Memory kept to be released later, somewhere else. Is that remembering or
                       releasing?                                      releasing; narrative
  the commons pasture  Ostrom's shared grazing: rules made by the users. What makes a rule a
                       covenant rather than a law?                     ordered-consensual
  the wiki talk page   Argument kept beside the article, never inside it. Is that a ledger, or a
                       telling?                                        narrative; CRITIQUE 1
  …                    (yours)

Suggested order for looking, with no runs: lichen (it bears on providers), the wolf pack (it
tests the caution), geese (rotation and rest), slime mould (knowing without a knower). Each
can be drawn into Part 3 as an entry, and anything it suggests goes into Part 2.
